  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Quality of TB care in DPR Korea - Korea (Democratic Peoples Republic) (01-Oct-2015-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Korea (Democratic Peoples Republic), Tuberculosis, United Nations Children&apos;s Fund (UNICEF)This program has the following goals: To decrease morbidity and mortality of TB through universal access to TB care and support service. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: Engage other health programmes, civil society, NGOs and Key affected population in TB control (Objective 3).  Objective 2: Scale up services for prevention, diagnosis and treatment of all forms of TB to achieve case notification rate of 444 per 100,000 population by 2018 and to sustain 90 % success rate for notified new smear positive cases (Objective 1).  Objective 3: To ensure timely enrolment of all confirmed MDR-TB and achieve 75% treatment success rate (Objective 2).  Objective 4: Contribute to Health System Strengthening based on Primary Health Care approach (Objective 4)</narrative>
  </description>
